  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, up to a maximum amount of P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this means that when calculating the estate tax, the value of the family home can be excluded from the total estate value, thereby reducing the taxable estate. This deduction is particularly beneficial for families, as it helps preserve the family home for the heirs and minimizes the estate tax liability.",
